---
import ShibaMascot from './ShibaMascot.astro';

// Role responsibilities and output paths match apps/frontend/src/employee-templates.ts.
// These original Shibas represent instruction templates, never models or providers.
const agents = [
  { character: 'marketing', name: 'Marketing', role: 'Draft a grounded brief and campaign assets for review.', deliverables: ['marketing/brief.md', 'marketing/campaign.md'] },
  { character: 'sales', name: 'Sales', role: 'Draft evidence-based outreach and account briefs for review.', deliverables: ['sales/account-brief.md', 'sales/outreach.md'] },
  { character: 'research', name: 'Research', role: 'Produce a sourced report with explicit gaps and uncertainty.', deliverables: ['research/report.md', 'research/sources.json'] },
  { character: 'product', name: 'Product', role: 'Turn evidence and requirements into a scoped product brief.', deliverables: ['product/brief.md', 'Scope, acceptance criteria and open questions'] },
  { character: 'design', name: 'Design', role: 'Draft accessible flows and interface copy grounded in the product.', deliverables: ['design/spec.md', 'States, keyboard behavior and acceptance checks'] },
  { character: 'engineering', name: 'Engineering', role: 'Implement a focused change with regression checks and a handoff.', deliverables: ['Task-scoped code and tests', 'Verification results and handoff'] },
  { character: 'operations', name: 'Operations', role: 'Write an actionable runbook with checks and recovery steps.', deliverables: ['operations/runbook.md', 'Readiness checks and recovery checklist'] },
  { character: 'custom', name: 'Your custom role', role: 'Save a named agent with instructions shaped around your organization’s work.', deliverables: ['Your instructions', 'Your expected deliverables'] },
] as const;
interface Props { size?: 'card' | 'hero'; }
const { size = 'card' } = Astro.props;
---
<section class:list={['agent-cast', { 'hero-cast': size === 'hero' }]} aria-label="Shiba employee role templates">
  <div class="cast-grid">
    {agents.map((agent, index) => (
      <article class="agent-card" data-character={agent.character}>
        <div class="card-top"><span class="template-label">{agent.character === 'custom' ? 'Configurable' : 'Template'}</span><span aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span></div>
        <div class="avatar"><ShibaMascot character={agent.character} size={size} /></div>
        <h3>{agent.name}</h3>
        <p class="role">{agent.role}</p>
        <div class="deliverables"><h4>{agent.character === 'custom' ? 'You define' : 'Typical deliverables'}</h4><ul>{agent.deliverables.map(deliverable => <li>{deliverable}</li>)}</ul></div>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="cast-notes">
    <p>Roles configure instructions and expected deliverables, not independent models. They use the harness and model selected for the run. Outputs depend on the task, supplied evidence and available access; a role does not grant external integrations or permission to publish.</p>
    <p>Planning may precede approval. Standard sandbox execution waits for approval; scoped unattended automation is an explicit opt-in exception. External sending, posting and production changes need supported access and approval for the exact action.</p>
    <a href="/docs/readiness/">Read the verification evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    <p class="readiness-note">Local adapter checks do not establish successful inference or cloud end-to-end execution.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .agent-cast { color: var(--ink, #222320); font-family: 'Geist', sans-serif; }
  .cast-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; }
  .agent-card { min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 24px; background: var(--card, #f6f4ed); border: 1px solid var(--hairline, var(--line-2, #a9aaa3)); border-radius: 16px; transition: border-color .25s ease, box-shadow .25s ease; }
  .agent-card:hover { border-color: var(--navy, #0000a8); box-shadow: 0 8px 24px color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 6%, transparent); }
  .card-top { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; color: var(--ink-2, var(--ink)); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .template-label { padding: 4px 9px; border: 1px solid var(--hairline, var(--line-2)); border-radius: 6px; }
  .avatar { width: 180px; max-width: 100%; min-height: 160px; display: grid; place-items: center; margin: 20px auto; }
  .hero-cast .cast-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .hero-cast .avatar { width: 240px; }
  .agent-card h3 { color: var(--ink); font: 400 26px/1.2 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .agent-card .role { color: var(--ink); font: 400 14px/1.75 'Geist', sans-serif; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .deliverables { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline, var(--line-2)); }
  .agent-card .deliverables h4 { color: var(--ink-2, var(--ink)); font: 500 11px/1.5 'Geist Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  ul { display: grid; gap: 8px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  li { color: var(--ink); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.65; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .cast-notes { max-width: 900px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .cast-notes p { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--ink-2, var(--ink)); }
  .cast-notes a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 44px; color: var(--navy); font-size: 13px; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .cast-notes a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--navy); outline-offset: 4px; border-radius: 2px; }
  .cast-notes .readiness-note { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .cast-grid, .hero-cast .cast-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .cast-grid, .hero-cast .cast-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; } .agent-card { padding: 24px; } .agent-card h3 { font-size: 24px; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .agent-card { transition: none; } }
</style>
